    "sp_why": {
      "type": "c-content-panel",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_why_text_0": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Every NANGA down product carries a certificate of origin stating where its down comes from. Products we used to label simply as “white duck down” now use Spanish white duck down exclusively. Until now, we blended down from France, Spain, Hungary, and elsewhere and labeled it “European.” So what's the advantage of narrowing the source from Europe as a whole to Spain alone?</p><p>“Today, most down on the market comes from Pekin ducks raised in China, but we mainly use European white duck down from France and Spain. For NANGA products, we've switched all of our raw down to Spanish,” says Masahiro Kawada of Kawada Feather, which processes the down for NANGA products.</p><p>Down's quality and performance depend not only on the breed of waterfowl, but also on how and how long the birds are raised. For this switch, Kawada traveled with NANGA President Tomoyuki Yokota to visit producers on a mountainside in Spain.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "sp_why_text_0"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "background_color": "#ffffff",
        "text_color": "#000000",
        "body_text_color": "#4b5563",
        "full_width": false
      }
    },
    "sp_landscape": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_land_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>“France has a long history of raising waterfowl and still uses traditional methods, so French down has a great reputation. But because that history is so long, when you actually visit the producers, the facilities often show their age.</p><p>Spanish producers are newer to the industry. They've installed modern equipment on large properties and raise their birds in a very clean, open environment. Even with that many birds, there's barely any smell. Between the facilities, the environment, and the scale of production, I expect Spanish down to keep gaining market share.”</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "sp_land_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/knowledge-spanish-down-landscape.jpg",
        "image_link": "",
        "full_width": false,
        "image_position": "right",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "sp_mature": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_mature_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Down is a by-product of the meat industry. Spain's main customers are countries like France that care deeply about food, so producers raise their ducks longer to improve the meat. That's another advantage of Spanish down.</p><p>Much Pekin down comes from young birds raised for less than 40 days, while Spanish ducks are raised for about 80. Larger, mature birds produce down that is stronger, more resilient, and higher lofting. The difference shows over time: products made with mature down flatten less and keep their loft through years of use.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "sp_mature_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/knowledge-spanish-down-farm-visit.jpg",
        "image_link": "",
        "full_width": false,
        "image_position": "left",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "sp_health": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_health_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>“Spain is also off the migration routes of wild birds, so it's less affected by avian influenza. The farms sit on mountainsides far from towns, so there's less risk of exposure to viruses. That environment is another advantage of Spanish down.”</p><p>This premium raw down is then turned into high-quality down by Kawada Feather, which has some of the best facilities and expertise in the world.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "sp_health_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
