    "sp_factory": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_fac_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Kawada Feather's factory is in Meiwa, in Japan's Mie Prefecture. The company chose the location for its dry climate and some of the softest water in Japan, ideal conditions for processing down.</p><p>“Clean down is essential to a high-quality down product. Using techniques refined over many years, we completely remove invisible dust and debris, along with the dirt and oils from the birds themselves. Clean down flattens less and lasts longer, and water-repellent treatments bond to it more easily. Because we remove the dust and allergens that harbor bacteria, it's also less likely to cause allergies.”</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "sp_fac_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/knowledge-spanish-down-cleaned.jpg",
        "image_link": "",
        "full_width": false,
        "image_position": "left",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "sp_wash": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_wash_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Here's how Kawada Feather refines down. Before washing, the raw down is dedusted to remove fine debris, oxidized oils, and sand. Getting the heavy dirt out here is key, Kawada says. About 20% of the dirt comes off at this stage.</p><p>The down is then washed in large drum machines with ultra-soft water and a down-specific detergent. Complex currents rub the clusters against each other, polishing the down the way you'd rinse rice. That's the Kawada method. He describes it as peeling one thin layer off the surface of each feather, and the washed down really does come out a shade whiter.</p><p>“We draw ultra-soft water, with a hardness of 3, from the Ōdaigahara mountains. Its fine particles mean we need less detergent, and it penetrates deep into the down to lift out fine dirt and oils. The slightly alkaline water also helps reverse oxidation and repair damaged areas of the down. It's the ideal water for processing down, which is why we moved our factory here.”</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "sp_wash_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/knowledge-spanish-down-factory.jpg",
        "image_link": "",
        "full_width": false,
        "image_position": "right",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "sp_dry": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_dry_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>After two washes and four rinses, the down is dried quickly at 140–150°C (284–302°F). Once it cools, it's dedusted again to remove the dirt, dust, and feather fragments loosened in the wash, then air is used to separate the down from the feathers.</p><p>The down is quality-tested, and only down that meets Kawada's in-house standards, which are stricter than those of the Japan Down Products Cooperative Association, moves on to final blending.</p><p>To keep quality consistent all year, down of the same species, origin, and grade from different lots is blended in a mixing machine. As a natural material, down varies in ways numbers don't capture, like how it lofts and how it holds up over time. Kawada's own techniques bring it to a consistent standard.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "sp_dry_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/knowledge-spanish-down-inspection.jpg",
        "image_link": "",
        "full_width": false,
        "image_position": "left",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "sp_close": {
      "type": "c-content-panel",
      "blocks": {
        "sp_close_text_0": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Down refined this way is known as “Kawada-standard down.” It's shipped to manufacturers in anti-static bags and made into apparel and comforters at factories in Japan and abroad.</p><p>“Down is made of hard keratin, so it's strong to begin with. It can last more than 100 years, and 200 if you keep washing it in soft water. It's a natural resource with remarkable performance. We want people to use it carefully for a long time, so we never compromise on quality. Our goal is to deliver down that's safe and that people can trust.”</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
